{{> Top frame}}
<header>
  <p class="kicker">Lesson 4</p>
  <h1>Lists</h1>
  <p class="lede">A section repeats for each element of a list, shows once for a true Bool,
  and an inverted one shows when the list is empty.</p>
</header>

<figure class="preview">
  <figcaption><code>templates/Menu.rocstache</code>, rendered</figcaption>
{{> Menu menu}}</figure>

<section class="turn-box">
  <h2>Your turn</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><p>In <code>main.roc</code>, add a dish to <code>dishes</code>:</p>
    <pre><code>{ name: "Hollandaise", price: 280 },</code></pre></li>
    <li><p>Now write the price as <code>"280"</code>, a string. The menu declared
    <code>price : U32</code>, so roc says so.</p></li>
    <li><p>Empty the list (<code>dishes = []</code>) and watch the inverted section.</p></li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Read <code>templates/Menu.rocstache</code></h2>
  <dl class="syntax">
    <dt><code>&#123;&#123;% Ctx : &#123; … &#125; %&#125;&#125;</code></dt><dd>the contract, declared; first in the file</dd>
    <dt><code>&#123;&#123;#dishes&#125;&#125; … &#123;&#123;/dishes&#125;&#125;</code></dt><dd>once per dish, its fields in scope</dd>
    <dt><code>&#123;&#123;^dishes&#125;&#125; … &#123;&#123;/dishes&#125;&#125;</code></dt><dd>when there are none</dd>
    <dt><code>&#123;&#123; dishes | len | plural "dish" "dishes" &#125;&#125;</code></dt><dd>formatters: <code>len</code>, <code>plural</code>, <code>upper</code>, <code>lower</code>, <code>url</code></dd>
  </dl>
  <p>Anything fancier is computed in Roc and handed over as a field. Templates stay dumb on
  purpose: the logic lives where the types are.</p>
</section>
